According to Article 19 of the Law No. 152-FZ, the data operator should take all reasonable organizational and technical measures when processing personal data in order to prevent unauthorized access to personal data, its destruction, alteration, blocking, copying, distribution or conduct of other illegitimate acts. 
Article 22.1 of the Law which has been in force since 2011 requires appointment of a person responsible for organizing the processing of personal data. This person is responsible for organizing the processing of personal data and should:
1) exercise internal control over compliance by the operator and its employees with the legislation of the Russian Federation concerning personal data, including requirements relating to the protection of personal data;
2) make employees of the operator aware of the provisions of the legislation of the Russian Federation concerning personal data, of by-laws on the processing of personal data and of requirements relating to the protection of personal data;
3) organize the acceptance and processing of applications and requests from data subjects or their representatives and (or) to exercise control over the acceptance and processing of such applications and requests.

