indicators.impact:
The trade secrets can be protected under the Unfair Competition Provisions of the Turkish Commercial Code, which states that disclosing manufacturing and business secrets that belong to others unlawfully constitutes unfair competition. Article 56 of the Commercial Code allows persons who have suffered damages or who may be exposed to the risk of such damage to apply to the competent court for the following:
- Declare as to whether the defendant's action is unfair;
- Prevent unfair competition;
- Removal of the material condition caused by the action of unfair competition; rectification of statement if the unfair competition is committed by wrong or misleading statements; and destruction of the means used in the unfair competition action, provided that it is unavoidable to prevent the infringement;
- In the case of a faulty action, compensation of damages; Should the conditions set forth by Article 58 of the Turkish Code of Obligations be met (i.e. damages to incur one’s personal rights), there will be compensation of non-pecuniary damages.

Criminal Code (Law No. 5237)
Article 239: Criminalizes the unauthorized disclosure of trade secrets, imposing penalties for violations.

